    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d168">

                <pb facs="0300" n="258" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg258"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 391.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-04-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 24, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I transmit a copy of a note from Lord
                    Russell to me, of the 21st instant, respecting the departure of the Japan, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">alias</hi> the Virginia. I have no reason to doubt the
                    correctness of the representations therein made of the condition <pb facs="0301"
                        n="259" xml:id="pg259"/> of that vessel. Indeed, this will account for the
                    fact that I had not myself received from any of the consuls information of her
                    readiness for a voyage until after she was gone.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d168-a1.xml" xpointer="d168-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
